---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Privacy — Hours Apart';
const description =
  'Hours Apart has no accounts, no database and no tracking cookies. Here is exactly what it does and does not keep.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/privacy">
  <article class="max-w-2xl">
    <header class="mb-7">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-4xl">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-paper-700">
        The short version: there is nothing to collect, because the site was built without a place
        to put it. No account, no database, no login.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What stays on your device</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper-700">
        Your list of cities is not stored on a server. It is encoded into the address bar, which is
        why you can bookmark it, reload it, or paste the link to someone else and have them see the
        same thing. The link never leaves your browser unless you choose to share it.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper-700">
        The only thing kept locally is your theme choice &mdash; whether you asked the page to
        follow your sky, or pinned it to light or dark. That lives in your browser's <span
          class="nums">localStorage</span
        > and goes no further. Clearing your site data removes it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Where the time data comes from</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper-700">
        Offsets, daylight saving rules and your local zone are read from your own device through the
        browser's built-in internationalisation API. Nothing about your location is sent anywhere to
        work out the time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper-700">
        The site sets no cookies and runs no advertising or cross-site tracking. Like any website it
        is served by a host (Cloudflare) that keeps standard, aggregate request logs for security
        and reliability; those are not tied to an identity here.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Changes</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-paper-700">
        If this ever changes &mdash; say a privacy-preserving, cookieless usage count is added
        &mdash; it will be described here first.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-10">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="ring-focus rounded text-sm font-medium text-paper-900 hover:text-paper-700"
      >
        &larr; Back to the world clock
      </a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
